    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>A federation of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-aragon">Aragon</a>, Catalonia, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/valencia">Valencia</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mallorca">Majorca</a> under one king, each realm keeping its own laws, Corts and coinage.</li><li>Its fleets won <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sicily">Sicily</a> in 1282, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sardinia">Sardinia</a> from 1323 and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/naples">Naples</a> in 1442, building an Iberian empire in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mediterranean">Mediterranean</a>.</li><li>United with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-castile">Castile</a> from 1479, it kept its separate institutions until the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nueva-planta-decrees">Nueva Planta decrees</a> of 1707–1716.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/james-i-of-aragon">James I</a> the Conqueror left an account of his own reign, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/llibre-dels-fets">Llibre dels fets</a>, one of the earliest autobiographies by a medieval Christian king.</p></aside>
    </section>

